  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Chamfer with no picks now refuses at generation when a top edge loop carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length.\nThe message names a point on the bevelled part and a point on the sharp part. It asks the user to pick the edges.\n\nExample text, from the unit test fixture: `the edge loop near X1.000 Y20.000 carries a modelled chamfer on only part of its length - it is sharp near X30.500 Y0.000 - a chamfer with no picks would cut the sharp part; pick the edges to break`.\n\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/chamfer_ride.rs`: the new function `partly_bevelled`, and one call in `ride_loops`.\n- `crates/app/tests/chamfer_partly_bevelled.rs`: the plate of the issue, with and without the extra vertex.\n- `docs/decisions/2887-chamfer-partly-bevelled.md`: the decision record.\n\nThe issue permits two results: a ride of the bevelled segments only, or a named refusal that asks for picks. This PR takes the refusal.\n\n## Cause\n\n`ride_loops` classified each top loop whole, by the farthest vertex from the wall loop.\nA loop that is bevelled on one side has two readings.\nWith an extra vertex on the top edge of the bevel, the loop read as bevelled. The ride then cut the three sharp sides.\nWithout that vertex, the two bevel corners lie on the wall, and the loop read as sharp. The tip then stood inside the part at the bevel.\nThe verifier refused the two programs as a gouge at a coordinate, with no reason.\n\n## The check\n\nThe check runs for each segment of the matched top loop. It measures the two ends and the middle against the wall loop.\n\n- A segment within 1e-6 mm of the wall is sharp.\n- A segment more than 0.05 mm from the wall is bevelled.\n- A segment between the two values counts as neither.\n\nThe loop is refused when it has a bevelled segment and more than one chamfer width of sharp length.\nThe result does not depend on tessellation.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n\n- `a_no_pick_chamfer_on_a_plate_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_by_name` (app, `chamfer_partly_bevelled`)\n- `the_refusal_does_not_depend_on_an_extra_vertex_on_the_bevel` (app, `chamfer_partly_bevelled`)\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_loop_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_by_name` (motion lib)\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_loop_bevelled_on_one_side_refuses_with_an_extra_vertex_too` (motion lib)\n- `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_loop_bevelled_all_round_is_not_partly_bevelled` (motion lib)\n\nMutation: with `chamfer_ride.rs` of `upstream/main` 17b1b2b81, the two app pins fail (`a partly bevelled edge loop with no picks is refused: ()`: generation succeeds). With the fix, the two pins pass.\nThe motion unit pins were not run against the old file: they call the new function, so the old file does not compile with them.\n\nUnchanged and green: the six older `chamfer_ride` unit tests and the seven tests of `chamfer_modelled_edge` (#303, #2435, #2596).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green on 7991bc04b (4 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Heavy review results\n\nVerified head: `7991bc04bba6db467460b375821a8ea30011786d`. No source changes were needed for the review finding.\n\n`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` passed: 223 steps, 0 failed, 47.6 minutes.\n\n- Release build: passed (1 step).\n- Motion heavy lane: passed (34 steps). Tests: 56 passed. Two registered failures for #1950 failed as expected.\n- App heavy lane: passed (188 steps). Tests: 42 passed. One registered failure for #1950 failed as expected.\n- No unexpected failure occurred. No golden file changed.\n\nThe three registered #1950 cases are:\n\n- Motion: `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_reaches_the_air_planner_with_the_stock`.\n- Motion: `machining2d::pocket_hsm::ring_tests::the_stock_ring_level_plans_adaptive_with_no_budget_note`.\n- App: `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 4 steps, 0 failed, 11.9 minutes.\nMotion lib: 477 passed, 10 ignored. `chamfer_modelled_edge`: 7 passed. `chamfer_partly_bevelled`: 2 passed.\n\n`cargo clippy -j 32 -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\nThe heavy run started with `upstream/main` at `0510ff382015bfb46f088c44436919c0b000de58`.\nThe quick run started with that ref at `7173bb44ac16512c1571fc58b804816e98712e68` after an external fetch.\nBoth bases give merge base `17b1b2b81c2fc555fdaa3f06dec73000d19d20c7` and the same three changed files.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` or `.cl` file changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A partial ride of only the bevelled segments is not in this PR. The decision record gives the reasons.\n- No note lists whole loops that a no-pick chamfer leaves sharp (the #2596 case). `ride_loops` has no warning channel. That is separate work.\n- Curved partly bevelled loops (a fillet on a part of an arc) have no test. The check uses three samples for each segment.\n- The verifier is not changed.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n`chamfer_ride.rs`: no open PR changes it.\n#2831 adds a field to `OpParams::Face` in each test file that builds it. The new test file here builds `OpParams::Face` too. The PR that merges second adds the field in `crates/app/tests/chamfer_partly_bevelled.rs`.\n\nWritten by an Opus lead + Haiku workers (lane trial)\n\n- Worker 1 (Haiku) wrote the guard and its unit tests, and its tests passed. The lead then lost that edit by accident during the mutation check: the copy to a save file was refused and the revert of the file ran. The lead wrote the guard again from the worker's reported diff, with small changes (`hypot`, an iterator loop, a shared fixture for the unit tests). So the lead wrote the 93 lines of `chamfer_ride.rs` that are in this PR, to the design that the lead gave the worker.\n- Worker 2 (Haiku) wrote `crates/app/tests/chamfer_partly_bevelled.rs` (145 lines) from the lead's mesh specification. The lead did not change it.\n- Worker 3 (Haiku) wrote the decision record (26 lines) from the lead's content. The lead did not change it.\n- In lines: workers 171 of 264 (65 %), lead 93 of 264 (35 %). The root cause, the design and the review are the lead's.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Chamfer with no picks on an edge loop that has a modelled chamfer on only part of its length now refuses by name and asks for picks; before, the post gate refused it as a gouge with no reason (#2887).\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2887\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
